cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite this repository.
title: >-
  Insomnia TCM Mining — Reproducible Experiment Package for Apriori
  Association Rule and Complex Network Analysis of Insomnia Traditional
  Chinese Medicine Prescriptions
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Junhua
    family-names: Li
    alias: lijunhua
version: 1.3.0
date-released: "2026-05-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ourHua/insomnia-tcm-mining"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.20267587"
    description: "Permanent Zenodo archive for v1.3.1"
  An end-to-end, single-command reproducible pipeline of eleven Python
  scripts, a Makefile and a continuous-integration workflow. Starting
  from two minimum-necessary CSV inputs containing only the fields
  prescription_id and herb, the pipeline regenerates every numerical
  result, eight figures and six tables. A third party can therefore
  independently verify the reported numbers with a single `make all`
  command.
keywords:
  - traditional Chinese medicine
  - insomnia
  - data mining
  - Apriori
  - association rules
  - complex network analysis
  - Louvain community detection
  - Leiden community detection
  - reproducible research
